 shutil.copy2(D/'all_attempts_video_audit_60/independent_audit.json',O/'video_audit.json');shutil.copy2(D/'force_schedule_recovery_82/recovery.json',O/'solver_recovery82.json');shutil.copy2(D/'actuator_path_recovery_75/recovery.json',O/'launch_recovery75.json')
 body=''.join('<tr><td>'+html.escape(r['study'])+'</td><td>'+html.escape(r['scope'])+'</td><td>'+f"{r['clearance_mm']:.4f}"+'</td><td>'+html.escape(str(r.get('command_time_s','—')))[:10]+'</td><td>'+('Endpoint only; no motion admitted' if r.get('endpoint_passed') else 'Rejected / incomplete')+'</td></tr>' for r in rows)
 page=f'''<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Low-seat repair: command filter and contact checks</title><style>body{{font:17px/1.55 system-ui;color:#203a44;background:#eef3f4;margin:0}}main{{max-width:1120px;margin:auto;padding:34px}}h1{{font-size:34px;line-height:1.2}}h2{{margin-top:34px}}.callout{{background:white;border-left:5px solid #a84235;padding:24px;border-radius:7px}}img,video{{width:100%;background:white}}table{{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;background:white;font-size:15px}}th,td{{text-align:left;padding:11px;border-bottom:1px solid #d1dade;vertical-align:top}}a{{color:#166781}}</style></head><body><main><h1>Physical repair remains unresolved</h1><div class="callout"><b>Best verified:64/72 clean,70 stable,8 slipping,2 housing contacts.</b><br>All64 successful conditions remain protected. No new physical trial, PPO update, fresh holdout or policy promotion occurred. Physical criteria and materials are unchanged.</div><h2>What the new checks show</h2><p>The corrected collision model and full joint-command checks now describe a sampled step-and-crouch approach. However, the complete filtered command and legal contact transition remain infeasible in the tested designs. The model searches are limited evidence, not proof that no solution exists.</p><img src="comparison.png" alt="Specific command timing and contact clearance for tested offline plans"><table><tr><th>Study</th><th>Model scope</th><th>Clearance mm</th><th>Command time s</th><th>Status</th></tr>{body}</table><p>Path80 fails one of105 dense foot-orientation checks and its command-time gate. Its small violation is retained, not rounded into a pass. For path77, optimizing only the assumed foot-corner force distribution reduces the specific command time from13.726 to13.482seconds. Initial/final commands, geometry, total foot-load schedule, joint margins, effort limits and0.15rad/s cap remain fixed.</p><h2>The real command filter prevents that nominal schedule</h2><img src="filter_check.png" alt="Command mismatch caused by the unchanged filter and target clamp"><p>The source filter clamps desired targets to the existing joint margin, applies0.1 filtering, then caps each20ms increment at0.003rad. A CPUfloat32 command-only replay clips47 inverse-filter targets. The largest command-path mismatch is{filt['max_command_path_difference_rad']:.6f}rad, with{filt['final_command_difference_rad']:.6f}rad remaining at the end. No such command was applied to physics. Timing alone does not make this an executable approach.</p><h2>Touchdown needs more clearance than hovering</h2><p>Path77 ends with a1mm pelvis gap. The new zero-gap transition84 checks21 unloaded approach knots followed by10 fixed-pose modeled-load knots. No seat force is assigned before contact. Housing clearance falls to{contact['summary']['minimum_housing_clearance_mm']:.4f}mm, below the unchanged3mm model screen. The modeled0.1BW normal seat force is an assumed equilibrium, not a measured contact.</p><p>Stance86 allows the lifted foot to land farther rearward and with bounded yaw. It reaches the120mm planning bound at2.954543mm clearance and remains FAILED. Revision89 extends only that internal distance bound to140mm; its best tested contact clearance is{last['summary']['housing_clearance_mm']:.4f}mm. No foot is dragged or teleported: these are endpoint hypotheses, and a new lifted-foot trajectory still has to be constructed and checked.</p><p><b>{summary['next']}</b></p><h2>All recorded physical attempts, including failures</h2><video controls preload="metadata" src="../all_attempts_video_v2_59/all_attempts.mp4"></video><p>The58.4-second H.264 video remains current because this round added no physical motion. It includes all32 recorded sources:696 complete20s trials (405 success,291 failure),72 recorded diagnostic prefixes, and static disclosure of72 aborted attempts without saved motion. The independent audit covers462 first-event samples. These repeated historical totals are not the best controller’s success rate.</p><p>Offline schematic from recorded XYZW/body transforms.0.1s pose samples bracket0.02s event labels; no fabricated motion.</p><h2>Effort, preservation and limitations</h2><p>{summary['effort']}</p><p>Independent audits replay geometry, finite-difference virtual work, balanced forces, joint/finger commands and timing. They retain every failed model gate. The first force LP82 stopped at a residual assertion; the preserved v2 tightens solver accuracy to1e−10 while retaining the validation limits and reporting residuals. No physical threshold, runtime or result array from earlier studies was altered.</p><p>Reference-assisted simulation on nearby rigid slabs does not establish unassisted sitting, real-robot validation, or sitting and leaning anywhere. Leaning has not broadened.</p><p><a href="summary.json">Detailed summary</a> · <a href="forces82_filter83_audit.json">Force and filter audit</a> · <a href="contact84_audit.json">Contact audit</a> · <a href="stance89_audit.json">Latest endpoint audit</a> · <a href="video_audit.json">Complete video coverage</a> · <a href="SHA256.json">SHA256 manifest</a></p></main></body></html>'''
 (O/'findings.html').write_text(page);(O/'SHA256.json').write_text(json.dumps({p.name:sha(p) for p in O.iterdir() if p.is_file()},indent=2));print(json.dumps(dict(report=str(O),entries=len(read(O/'SHA256.json')),task_complete=False)))
